.SH "NAME"
roark\-dashboard\-update \- Update a dashboard
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark dashboard update
\fIdashboard\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Edits a dashboard. Omitted fields keep their current value. `widgets`, when sent, replaces the list: widgets are matched by name, so a widget that keeps its name keeps its id; a new name adds a widget and a name no longer listed removes it. To change one widget, PUT /v1/dashboard/{dashboardId}/widget/{widgetId}.
.SH "API"
PUT /v1/dashboard/{dashboardId}
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIdashboard\-id\fR
